# ALL.wantrc — DECLARED exit codes for entries whose CORRECT run exits nonzero.
# Format: name<TAB>rc   ·   blank lines and # comments ignored   ·   rc=0 is the default and is REFUSED here.
# See tests/prolog/ALL.wantrc for the convention this file follows.
#
# simple_output_25 (origin ladder__rung07_refuse_field_of_nonrecord): calling a DATA()-generated field
# accessor (x(...)) on a value that is not a `point` record is a runtime "Error 5: Undefined function or
# operation" (SNOBOL4-shared runtime dispatch) -- SCRIP prints "before" to stdout (confirmed the accessor
# call itself, not the preceding statement, is what fails) then the diagnostic to STDERR only, and both m3
# and m4 exit rc=1 with stdout byte-identical (7 bytes, "before\n"). This is the rung07 REFUSE witness; see
# task LEDGER for rung06's zero-byte-output trap this design deliberately avoids.
simple_output_25	1
#
# alt_replace_3 (origin ladder__rung09_refuse_alt_as_number): `1 | 2 | 3` outside a scan/pattern context
# is a genuine SNOBOL4 PATTERN value (TT_ALT lowers to the native pattern-alternation operator, not an
# Icon-style generator -- confirmed empirically: `x := 1|2|3; OUTPUT := x` prints "PATTERN", the datatype
# name), so comparing it numerically (`= 2`) is a type error: "Error 101: eq first argument is not
# numeric" on stderr, rc=1 both modes (m4: the COMPILE step exits 0 as expected -- this is a RUNTIME
# error -- the emitted BINARY exits rc=1 when run, confirmed). stdout unaffected at "before\n".
alt_replace_3	1
#
# len_capture_1 (origin ladder__rung10_refuse_len_wrong_type): LEN() takes an integer length, not a
# string -- LEN("abc") is "Error 120: len argument is not integer or expression" on stderr, rc=1 both
# modes (m4: compile succeeds, the emitted binary exits 1 when run). stdout unaffected at "before\n".
len_capture_1	1
